            "text": "An issue occurs when `echo_via_pager` (or command execution) closes stdout/stderr before command completion. Calling `flush()` on a closed stream in the `finally` block raises `ValueError: I/O operation on closed file`.\n\nTo fix this regression, we safely handle `(ValueError, OSError)` when flushing `sys.stdout` and `sys.stderr`.\n\n```edit\nFILE: src/click/testing.py\n\u003c\u003c\u003c\u003c\u003c\u003c\u003c SEARCH\n            finally:\n                sys.stdout.flush()\n                sys.stderr.flush()\n=======\n            finally:\n                try:\n                    sys.stdout.flush()\n                except (ValueError, OSError):\n                    pass\n                try:\n                    sys.stderr.flush()\n                except (ValueError, OSError):\n                    pass\n\u003e\u003e\u003e\u003e\u003e\u003e\u003e REPLACE\n```",
